// PARAM: --analysis congruence --context entry-state
// Context sensitivity for Congruence. Two call sites reach twice with the
// singleton entry classes 3 and 5; keying the callee by its entry state
// keeps them apart, so each activation returns a singleton and both checks
// are decided.
//
// The context-insensitive run of this same program is the paired
// imprecision case (../known-imprecision/05-context_join_loses_singleton
// .vimp): one shared context joins 3 and 5 into 3 (mod 2), the return is
// 2 (mod 4), and congruence_eqb declines on a non-singleton.
//
// The registry publishes Congruence under entry-state and call-string
// contexts, both resolving to the always-join solver: widening for
// congruence is plain join, and a strictly ascending chain of residue
// classes is a chain of proper divisors of the modulus, so join alone
// already terminates.
void twice(p) { return p * 2 }
void main() {
  a := twice(3);
  b := twice(5);
  __voblint_check(a == 6); // PROVED
  __voblint_check(b == 10) // PROVED
}
